{
  "evidence_boundary": "Held-out post-capture active-membership differential for ship-to-ship capture continuations. The initial site universe is reconstructed from owner-current T-1 positions plus the already validated special-movement overlay. Factual VCRs up to and including capture VCR N are treated as elapsed queue history: deterministic replay supplies terminal state, and production apply_ship_terminal_batch performs destroy/survivor/capture mutation atomically. Capture owner/race transfer is derived from the captor in VCR N; VCR N+1 is never used for mutation. After mutation, foreign candidates are rebuilt from active membership, current owner identity, T-1 orders for ships whose owner has not changed, and independently calibrated diplomacy. Any non-prize candidate whose owner changed earlier in the queue fails closed because persistence of its pre-capture orders is not assumed. The factual next opponent id is used only as the final comparator. This gate does not yet claim complete post-capture pair recomposition or left/right side prediction.",
